codex
The code-level trace has exposed one contract-sensitive edge worth probing: a single batch line containing multiple present observers plus an empty observer is currently classified only as “mixed,” which may suppress the required absent/empty class and its spelling census. I’m also testing resume honesty, because the prefix comparison presently checks kind/observer/origin/body but not the draft’s `authored_at` or outer `signature`.
